# FAIL CLOSED. The repo-root .gitignore has `.env`, which matches a file named
# exactly `.env` — it does NOT match `imagineering.env`. So before this file, a
# plaintext sibling dropped in this directory was fully committable, in a PUBLIC
# repo, next to its own ciphertext. Found by testing it rather than reading the
# pattern (`git check-ignore -v deploy/secrets/imagineering.env` → not ignored).
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit only the artifacts that belong here. An allowlist
# fails closed on the thing nobody predicted; a denylist only stops what someone
